cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "OpenSol: GPU multiphysics simulation"
version: 0.3.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lars504/OpenSol"
authors:
  - family-names: Madsen
    given-names: Lars S.
    affiliation: The University of Queensland
abstract: >-
  GPU (cupy) and CPU 1D / 2D / 3D multiphysics simulation: FDTD and FDFD
  electromagnetics, eigenmode expansion, waveguide modes, heat conduction,
  electric currents and electrostatics, magnetostatics and AC magnetic fields,
  semiconductor drift-diffusion, solid mechanics, elastic waves and laminar
  flow, and their couplings. Models are JSON files that a GUI, a headless API
  and a CLI all read; FEM on triangles and tetrahedra for the physics that
  declare them.
keywords:
  - multiphysics
  - GPU
  - FDTD
  - FDFD
  - finite element method
  - electromagnetics
  - optomechanics
  - photonics
